{"type":"message","id":"eb0b5f29","parentId":"1fc66dc2","timestamp":"2026-10-17T22:50:30.722Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed `parse_date` in `dates/parse.py`, and all 3 tests in `tests/test_parse.py` now pass.\n\n**Cause:** the format `\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S\"` has nothing for the trailing `Z`, so `strptime` raised \"unconverted data remains: Z\".\n\n**Fix:** I replaced it with `datetime.fromisoformat(s)`. On Python 3.11 and later (this environment runs 3.13.5), that reads `Z` and numeric offsets.\n\nWhat changes for callers:\n- **Timezones:** input ending in `Z` now returns a UTC-aware datetime, while input without one still returns a naive datetime, so `test_naive` and `day_key` behave as before. Comparing or subtracting an aware value against a naive one raises `TypeError`, so any caller that mixes the two from the feed will need to handle that.\n- **More formats accepted:** the function also takes forms the old format rejected, such as fractional seconds (`...:00.123`), offsets (`+02:00`) and date-only strings.\n- **Python version:** this needs Python 3.11 or later, since earlier versions of `fromisoformat` reject `Z`."}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"vertex-anthropic","model":"claude-opus-5-5","usage":{"input":2,"output":400,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":26760,"totalTokens":27162,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0},"cttl":{"ephemeral5m":26760}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1792277425824,"responseId":"msg_vrtx_011Cg8dL24LUCo3tp7LRjDsh","duration":4897.032573,"ttft":4870.286807,"contextSnapshot":{"promptTokens":26762,"nonMessageTokens":21589,"compactionEpoch":0}}}
